      "message": "That is a good idea and I refactored so that keystone/bin/keystone-all, keystone/cli.py, and keystone/httpd/keystone.py all use /keystone/openstack/common/log as logging. The problem is that there are some things in /keystone/common/logging.py that might not be in keystone/openstack/common/log.py, see trace pertaining to global log level: \n\nhttp://paste.openstack.org/show/43707/\n\nSo if we just switch out the setup_logging function with setup from keystone/openstack/common/log.py then we would be fine. If we implement keystone/openstack/common/log as logging in keystone/cli.py, keystone/httpd/keystone.py and keystone/bin/keystone-all then there are some assumed operations of the old implementation (keystone/common/logging.py). \n\nWondering how we should proceed with this. This might require us to make some changes to Oslo\u0027s logging module given the current implementation of logging in Keystone.",
